BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Spring and the River) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  In the first days, there lived a Spring at the mountain's crown and a River in the valley belo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    w. Each dawn, the Spring received five drops of starlight from the heavens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  The Spring faced a choice: hold the starlight for herself, or let it flow downward. She knew t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    hat any drops she released would gather strength on the mountain slopes, multiplying threefo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    ld by the time they reached the River.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  At first, the Spring was afraid. "If I give, I will have nothing," she whispered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  But wisdom came to her in a dream: "What flows returns.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  So the Spring released her starlight. Three drops became nine in the River's basin. The River,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (     grateful and abundant, sent back six drops through underground paths to replenish the Sprin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    g.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  Both were enriched.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  The Spring learned that giving with trust brought greater returns than hoarding in fear. The R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    iver learned that generosity toward one's benefactor sustained the cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  Season after season, they shared this dance. The Spring gave freely because she trusted. The R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (    iver returned generously because abundance should flow both ways.) Tj ET
