BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  In ancient times, two sibling rivers flowed from opposite mountains-the River of Giving and th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    e River of Return. Each spring, the Elder Mountain would bestow five golden seeds upon the R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    iver of Giving.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  The River faced a choice: keep the seeds safe within its banks, or send them downstream to whe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    re the rivers met. If sent, the Valley of Abundance would transform each seed into three, an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    d the River of Return would carry them back to share.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  At first, the River of Giving held tight to its seeds, fearing loss. But one spring, it releas) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    ed all five seeds into the current. The Valley worked its magic, multiplying them to fifteen) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    . The River of Return, seeing this gift of trust, returned ten seeds, keeping only five.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  Both rivers swelled with abundance-the River of Giving now held ten seeds instead of five, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (     the River of Return held five where it had none.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  The pattern continued through countless seasons. When trust flowed freely and returns matched ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    generosity, both rivers flourished. The valley bloomed eternal, teaching all who witnessed: ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    abundance multiplies when trust flows both ways, and prosperity is a river that must flow to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (     grow.) Tj ET
