BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      In the first days, there lived a Spring at the mountain's crown and a River in the valley ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (        below. Each dawn, the Spring received five drops of starlight from the heavens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      The Spring faced a choice: hold the starlight for herself, or let it flow downward. She kn) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (        ew that any drops she released would gather strength on the mountain slopes, multiplying) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (         threefold by the time they reached the River.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      At first, the Spring was afraid. "If I give, I will have nothing," she whispered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      But wisdom came to her in a dream: "What flows returns.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      So the Spring released her starlight. Three drops became nine in the River's basin. The Ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        ver, grateful and abundant, sent back six drops through underground paths to replenish t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        he Spring.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
