BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Spring and the River) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      In the first days, there lived a Spring at the mountain's crown and a River in the valley ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        below. Each dawn, the Spring received five drops of starlight from the heavens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      The Spring faced a choice: hold the starlight for herself, or let it flow downward. She kn) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        ew that any drops she released would gather strength on the mountain slopes, multiplying) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (         threefold by the time they reached the River.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      At first, the Spring was afraid. "If I give, I will have nothing," she whispered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      But wisdom came to her in a dream: "What flows returns.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      So the Spring released her starlight. Three drops became nine in the River's basin. The Ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        ver, grateful and abundant, sent back six drops through underground paths to replenish t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        he Spring.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      Both were enriched.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      The Spring learned that giving with trust brought greater returns than hoarding in fear. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        he River learned that generosity toward one's benefactor sustained the cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      Season after season, they shared this dance. The Spring gave freely because she trusted. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        he River returned generously because abundance should flow both ways.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      And so the mountain bloomed, and the valley flourished, and both understood: **the path to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (         plenty is paved with trust and reciprocity.**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
