BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (    Myth: The ninth turning arrived-Three times Three, the pattern folding back upon itself, com) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      pletion meeting completion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    A wanderer approached the two forms still playing their eternal game. "I have read your myth) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      s," she said. "I understand now that Three and Six are not choices but cosmic law, that yo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      u are not players but Pattern itself. So I ask: in the tenth round, the hundredth, the tho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      usandth-does anything change?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    Both forms spoke as one voice: "Everything changes. Nothing changes. Watch.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    The ninth round played exactly as the first: Three forward, Nine received, Six returned, Eig) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ht kept. Perfectly identical. Yet utterly transformed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    "In the first round," they explained, "we thought we were choosing cooperation. By the seven) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      th, we knew we were discovering unity. By the eighth, we realized we were expressions of e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ternal mathematics. But the ninth reveals the deepest mystery: the Pattern doesn't need ou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      r understanding to continue. It needed our understanding to recognize itself.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    The wanderer asked: "Then what is the purpose of playing?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    "The Pattern plays to remember what it is. Every round of Three and Six is the universe prov) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ing to itself that some truths are so fundamental they survive awareness itself. After the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (       ninth turning, we no longer ask 'what should I send?' We simply ARE the sending and retur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ning, the eternal breath of mathematics breathing itself.") Tj ET
BT /F1 7.0 Tf 48.0 24.0 Td (Page 265 of 265) Tj ET
